            <ArticleTitle>Unusual presentation of subretinal cysticercosis with hypopyon uveitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e17-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3928/01913913-20150311-13</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Subretinal cysticercosis presenting with anterior uveitis and hypopyon is rare. A 7-year-old boy presented with pain and hypopyon in the right eye. Ultrasonography showed a cystic lesion with scolex. Because visual prognosis was poor, he was treated conservatively. Timely diagnosis would facilitate early therapy and prevent visual loss.</AbstractText>
